# Environment Configuration Rules

## Centralized Env Access (B1)
All environment variable access **must go through `src/utils/env.ts`**. Never read `import.meta.env` in components.

When adding a variable:
1. Add it to `src/utils/env.ts`.
2. Declare it in `src/vite-env.d.ts` (`ImportMetaEnv`).
3. Add it to `.env.example` (no real secret).

## Three Environments (B2)

| Mode | File | Script |
|------|------|--------|
| `development` | `.env.development` | `npm run dev` |
| `staging` | `.env.staging` | `npm run dev:stage` |
| `production` | `.env.production` | `npm run build` |

Client-exposed vars **must** be prefixed `VITE_`. Secrets go in `.env.local` (git-ignored).
